```ADD_PAPER
2504.07611v1
This paper introduces Conditional Conformal Risk Adaptation (CRA), an extension of conformal prediction that focuses on delivering distribution-free risk guarantees for complex tasks such as medical image segmentation. CRA innovates by proposing a new score function and a dedicated probability calibration framework, which together provide adaptive prediction sets that yield tight conditional risk control. The experimental results are particularly compelling: the method is rigorously evaluated on polyp segmentation tasks, where it demonstrates significantly improved conditional risk bounds and more consistent performance across heterogeneous image groups. By achieving risk control that is tight up to an O(1/n) factor, the paper suggests that such adaptive strategies could inform the design of data-conditional methods that integrate Bayesian quadrature formulations with conformal prediction frameworks. This integration has the potential to further maximize reliability and tighten risk guarantees by leveraging the probabilistic interpretation and error quantification capabilities intrinsic to Bayesian quadrature.
``` 
~~~~~~~~~~~
