```ADD_PAPER
2502.13228v2
This work re-envisions conformal prediction by integrating Bayesian quadrature principles to furnish distribution-free, data‐conditional risk guarantees. The paper develops a framework where uncertainty in the integration process is quantified, leading to tight risk guarantees—tight up to an O(1/n) factor—even under finite-sample conditions. Experimental evaluations are rigorously presented, showing that this Bayesian reformulation offers improved reliability in risk estimates compared to traditional frequentist approaches. The algorithmic innovations demonstrated include the use of Bayesian quadrature to produce interpretable error bounds and adaptive prediction sets, thereby directly addressing the challenge of maximizing both the reliability and tightness of risk control in a data-driven setting.
``` 
